umptions.value_diffusion"],"boundary":"This applied helper identifies the Parisi value before any substitution of groundStateValue. Its own declaration explicitly assumes strip regularity, gradient contact, and the unit curvature moment, supplied by the recorded application. The penalty here is the full integral. Authored correspondence to inspected frozen source; unverified status is retained. No fresh Lean build, elaborated dependency extraction, axiom audit, Comparator acceptance, or independent mathematical acceptance is claimed.","citation_ids":["scalar-r2-13-cite-terminal-parisi-assembly"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"scalar.source_terminal_parisi_assembly","kind":"claim","label":"Terminal formulas at the Parisi value after concrete suppliers","locator":"Evolution/IntegralPrimitiveTerminal.lean:37–79; IsDiffusion.parisi_value_assembly; application in ContactAssembly.lean:41–42,54–55,70","source_id":"scalar-r2-13-source-terminal-assembly","statement":"For every minimizer gamma and supplied diffusion X on W, there exists U with the stopped-gradient martingale, almost-sure |U|≤1, U²=1 and full t→1− gradient convergence, mean-square convergence to U, parisi W gamma = E|X_1|−∫₀¹t gamma(t)dt = E[U B_1] = ∫₀¹E curvature(t,X_t)dt, interval integrability, and cutoff convergence of that integral to parisi W gamma.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.source_terminal_parisi_assembly","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.source_terminal_parisi_assembly","id":"field:0939fbc41a8adc34de70a82dc935512471d16b7b5bf96a142525c4041d1fdcd6","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.source_terminal_parisi_assembly","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a